  "auditor": "trapi:gpt-5.6-sol_2026-07-09",
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The proposed untreated alloy contains W, Mo, Ta, Nb, V, and a minor Al addition but no Y.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The intervention is addition of approximately 1 at% Y during alloy synthesis.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Approximately 1 at% Y will segregate to the oxide/metal interface during high-temperature oxidation.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Y segregation will enhance the adhesion of the oxide scale.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Y segregation will promote formation of a continuous Al2O3-rich mixed oxide scale.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Al-containing high-entropy alloys can form protective or continuous oxide layers that inhibit further oxidation.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC9787501::web::003::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The scale formed on the proposed Y-doped RHEA will be primarily Al2O3.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6513993::web::013::discussion",
        "PMC9787501::web::003::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Y acts through the reactive element effect in this alloy.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Interfacial Y reduces oxide grain-boundary diffusion.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Interfacial Y reduces void formation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Improved oxide-scale integrity limits oxygen ingress and slows further oxidation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6513993::web::013::discussion",
        "PMC9787501::web::003::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "At 1000°C in air for 100 hours, the Y-doped alloy will exhibit at least 30% less weight gain than the untreated alloy.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Y-doped alloy will exhibit significantly less oxide-scale spallation than the untreated alloy.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Approximately 1 at% Y will leave the alloy's mechanical properties largely unaffected.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Existing literature on the untreated standard RHEA typically reports higher oxidation weight gain and significant oxide-scale discontinuities at 1000°C in air for 100 hours.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The predicted improvement is expected under isothermal exposure to air at 1000°C for 100 hours.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Changing oxygen partial pressure, temperature, or exposure duration may change the intervention's benefit.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    }
